    "result": "I fixed the regression with a one-word change in `sqlparse/filters/reindent.py`. I haven't run the tests, so the fix is unconfirmed. The permission prompt blocked my test command, and I didn't retry it.\n\nThe condition in `_process_identifierlist` was missing a `not`. It read `tlist.within(sql.Values)` where it should read `not tlist.within(sql.Values)`. With the check inverted, the reindent line-splitting for identifier lists ran only inside `VALUES` clauses instead of everywhere else. That would explain why `select foo, ...` stayed on one line when the expected output puts each identifier on its own line.\n\nTo check it, run `pytest tests -q` from the workspace. The 15 reported checks should pass again."
  },
